  "rationale": [
    "The current erasure preserves the actual aligned Core forall/lambda prefix as a known declaration's flat entry and represents returned function values with canonical unary groups. It no longer introduces arbitrary result-arrow eta parameters.",
    "Ten JavaScript call sites passed returned-function arguments in the old flat entry call. Replace only their explicit parentheses/grouping according to the raw source prefix inventory below. No dynamic arity dispatch, retry or intermediate closure .length inspection is used.",
    "The three tail fixture definitions inspect their sole fuel/list entry argument before returning state closures. Their unchanged source therefore has entry arity 1 and does not satisfy the flat tail-loop recognizer. The old no-general-implementation expectations depended on the removed result eta. The corrected assertions positively require an exported arity-1 entry and the general returned-function route.",
    "Moving state lambdas in front of the source match would remove the frontend's raw-root structural recursion eligibility; adding state headers would invoke normalization to a private worker plus public call wrapper. Neither is an authorized assertion-preserving fixture substitution, so all six raw fixture files remain byte-identical.",
    "Eligible tail optimization remains a separate requirement. Root assigned a companion additive flat-IR tail swap/fuel/reverse block to the existing IR conformance compilation. This replay candidate alone is not a claim that positive tail optimization was executed or qualified."
  ],
